   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Don't do that",
     "texto": [
      "To say that something should not be done, use **-지 마세요** (please don't…). It is added to the verb stem: 가다 → **가지 마세요**, 앉다 → **앉지 마세요**, 만지다 → **만지지 마세요**.",
      "여기서 사진 찍**지 마세요** = please don't take photos here."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Polite instructions",
     "texto": [
      "To give a polite instruction, use **-(으)세요**: 가다 → **가세요**, 앉다 → **앉으세요**, 만지다 → **만지세요**. In the regular pattern, a stem ending in a vowel takes **-세요** and one ending in another consonant takes **-으세요**. If the stem ends in **ㄹ**, that ㄹ is dropped: 살다 → **사세요** (live). The form can also express advice or an invitation, depending on the context."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
